!panic: fixedbugs2494aheroesfunctionachandlerreachesthroughforkisrefused.before_fork was called from inside a signal handler: C called it while handling a signal, where neither this runtime's memory nor the C library's is safe to use. No function of the program is a signal handler, nor called by one: after `hero_net_catch_stop() -> i64` (`hero_net.h`), Ctrl-C and SIGTERM only make `hero_net_stop_asked() -> i64` answer 1 and a waiting call of that layer answer stopped; `hero_signal_watch(sig: i32) -> i64` (`hero_os.h`) counts any other signal, and `hero_signal_take(sig: i32) -> i64` gives the count since its last call
